    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d839">

                <pb facs="0111" n="1493" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v13p2/pg1493"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">S/S–NSC files, lot 63 D 351. NSC 5405 Series</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Secretary of Defense</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Executive Secretary of
                        the National Security Council</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lay</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-05-06">May 6, 1954</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>Subject:</label>
                    <item>Suspension of U.S. Military Aid to Indochina in Event of a Cease
                        Fire</item>
                </list>
                <p>Forwarded herewith, for the consideration of the National Security Council at an
                    early date, are the recommendations of the Joint Chiefs of Staff, on the above
                    subject, with which I concur.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d839-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">C. E.
                                Wilson</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d839-a1.xml" xpointer="d839-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d839-f1" n="1" xml:id="d839-f1-content">
                <p>The recommendations of the Joint Chiefs of Staff were approved by the National
                    Security Council at its 196th Meeting, May 8; for the memorandum of the
                    discussion at that meeting, see <ref target="#pg1505">p. 1505</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
